# p_9c2d — Guitar for the Crowd: Hana plays when friends are over

On a regular weekday, the guitar stays on the bedroom floor (bedroom_floor_b1) all evening. The Tuesday 20:00 pass confirmed it there, and the mixture's prediction of ON_PERSON at 20:00 was wrong. But when friends are over, the social dynamic changes: Hana's hobby is guitar, and a group of friends in the living room is the natural audience. The guitar comes out of the bedroom and is either being played (ON_PERSON) or set up on the coffee table for the group to listen to. This happens in the living room social window, roughly 19:30 to 22:00, after dinner is cleared.

This is the key differentiator from the regular weekday: on Tuesday the guitar was at bedroom_floor_b1 at 20:00 and 22:00. On Wednesday with friends, it should be in the living room. The p_a3f1 claim that the guitar is on the bedroom floor at 17–19h was confirmed on Tuesday, but that window is before the friends arrive; the social window 19:30–22:00 is where the difference shows.

Refuted if on Wednesday between 19:30 and 22:00 the guitar is found on the bedroom floor (Hana did not bring it out), or if it is in the bedroom at 21:00 (the social gathering did not include guitar).

