# p_5a6e — The Social Override: Wednesday evening displaces the two-person TV routine

This document captures the full Wednesday-evening override of the standard two-person routine. On a normal weekday (like Tuesday), the 22:00 pass finds both residents in the living room with the remote and blanket on the coffee table and mug_priya on the coffee table — a two-person TV-and-tea session. On Wednesday with friends, that pattern is displaced: the remote stays at the TV stand (no TV), the blanket is on the couch (guests sitting), the mugs are at the kitchen table (tea served at the table, not carried to the couch), and the water bottle is at the kitchen table (Hana's drink during the meal). The transition from kitchen to living room happens at 19:00–19:30 rather than the usual 21:00–22:00, because the group moves to the living room after dinner while the kitchen is still being cleaned.

This differs from p_7e3a (which focuses on the living-room objects) and p_4f8b (which focuses on the kitchen). This document is about the TRANSITION: the timing shift and the fact that the two-person TV objects (remote, blanket, mug_priya) do NOT migrate to the coffee table on Wednesday.

Refuted if on Wednesday at 22:00 the remote is on the coffee table AND the blanket is on the coffee table (the normal two-person TV pattern is intact, meaning no social override), or if mug_priya is on the coffee table at 21:00 (Priya is doing her usual two-person tea, not serving a group).

